#####
### Title: Suffix Array Construction, Burrows–Wheeler Transform (BWT), Inverse BWT, and Partial Suffix Arrays

**Input format:**  
- `text`: a string to be indexed.  
  • If the sentinel `$` is missing, it is appended automatically.  
- `K`: integer specifying the sampling interval for the partial suffix array.  
- Example input file:  
  Line 1 — text  
  Line 2 — integer K

**Objective of the functions:**  
- `suffixes_with_positions()`  
  Constructs the **naive suffix array** by:  
  • generating all suffixes of `text`,  
  • sorting them lexicographically,  
  • returning a data frame of `(position, suffix)` pairs.  
  Positions are reported in **0‑based indexing**, matching the Coursera convention.

- `bwt()`  
  Computes the **Burrows–Wheeler Transform** using the suffix array:  
  • For each suffix array position `i`, output the character preceding that suffix  
    (or the last character if the suffix begins at position 1).  
  • Returns the BWT string.

- `inverse_bwt_df()`  
  Reconstructs the original text from its BWT using the **LF‑mapping**:  
  • Builds the first column by sorting the BWT characters,  
  • Computes occurrence counts for both columns,  
  • Matches `(char, occurrence)` pairs to build LF‑mapping,  
  • Walks backward from the `$` sentinel to recover the original string.  
  Returns the reconstructed text.

- `partial_suffix_array()`  
  Computes a **K‑sampled suffix array**:  
  • Builds the full suffix array (0‑based),  
  • Outputs only entries where the suffix start position is divisible by `K`,  
  • Each output line contains:  
    `i  sa[i]`  
    where `i` is the suffix array index (0‑based) and `sa[i]` is the text position.

**Output format:**  
- `suffixes_with_positions()` returns a data frame with columns:  
  • `position`: 0‑based suffix start,  
  • `suffix`: the suffix string.  
- `bwt()` returns a single BWT string.  
- `inverse_bwt_df()` returns the original text including `$`.  
- `partial_suffix_array()` returns a list of `"i sa[i]"` strings suitable for writing to file.

**Coursera module:**  
Bioinformatics IV — Week 1–2 (Suffix Arrays, BWT, FM‑Index Construction)
